      "problem": "Find the axis of symmetry for the parabola $y=2{x}^{2}+8x-3.$",
      "worked_solution": "The equation of the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=a{x}^{2}+bx+c$ is given by\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{b}{2a}.\n$$\n\nWe substitute $a=2$ and $b=8$ into the formula for the axis of symmetry. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{8}{2(2)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{4} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the axis of symmetry is $x=-2.$",
